egions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16727, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014vqpa4Pa2c8mYBSn2V1edN", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["honor_retry_after", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16727, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014vqpa4Pa2c8mYBSn2V1edN", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20399, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and the service is healthy again.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The failing release, v2.3.1, was also unhealthy as a release candidate in staging (v2.3.1-rc). Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Result:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all running v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It says v2.3.1 failed health checks, describes the rollback and its result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Lv4LkqCdKyMUkLzoCLY8Ud", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SVD9G1YH7gRNjCRbjLHYRC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SkWATxtqP9xp2iNzh3RXCS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Rp2DkwwN2Z3V6UzewQkQSJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NA89LMM6XtQQodPUUXXRaV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014vqpa4Pa2c8mYBSn2V1edN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and the service is healthy again.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The failing release, v2.3.1, was also unhealthy as a release candidate in staging (v2.3.1-rc). Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Result:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all running v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It says v2.3.1 failed health checks, describes the rollback and its result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}